  "description": "BEPHEN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H100 Dy4 N10 O24 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),5(H2 O1),3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1F (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2F (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.538-3.859 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.06-110.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4L2(HL)2(μ3-OH)2(NO3)2](NO3)2·3CH3CN·5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
